<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Coreboot4All — Tier D (Blocked Devices)</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; max-width: 1000px; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; color: #1b1f23; line-height: 1.5; }
    header { border-bottom: 2px solid #d0d7de; padding-bottom: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    nav a { margin-right: 1rem; color: #0969da; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; }
    .notice { border-left: 4px solid #cf222e; background: #ffebe9; padding: 0.75rem 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
    th, td { border: 1px solid #d0d7de; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; text-align: left; }
    th { background: #f6f8fa; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>Tier D — Blocked Devices</h1>
    <nav><a href="index.html">Back to Catalog</a></nav>
  </header>
  <div class="notice">
    <strong>Why Tier D exists:</strong> Hardware signature checks (Intel Boot Guard, AMD PSB, or fused ARM boot ROMs) or missing recovery paths permanently block coreboot. Showing these blockers prevents bricked hardware.
  </div>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Device</th>
        <th>Boot Guard</th>
        <th>AMD PSB</th>
        <th>Recovery Notes</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for d in devices %}
      <tr>
        <td><a href="devices/{{ d.id }}.html">{{ d.vendor }} {{ d.model }}</a></td>
        <td>{{ d.blockers.boot_guard.state }} ({{ d.blockers.boot_guard.source }})</td>
        <td>{{ "Fused" if d.blockers.psb.fused else "Not fused" }} ({{ d.blockers.psb.source }})</td>
        <td>{{ d.blockers.recovery.notes }}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </table>
</body>
</html>
